{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630423-nightshade-veil-how-would-you-rule-it-works","id":630423,"title":"NIghtshade / Veil - How would you rule it works....","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-08-17T16:48:04-07:00","id":630423,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> NIghtshade / Veil - How would you rule it works....","content":"So, situation is this. A PC activated a Nightshade talen, tuning himself into shadow and therefore virtually invisible in his dark small room. Problem is, in a few seconds SWAT will break open the door and search the room.<br /> <br /> What do they see in the room once it is illuminated by lights they have under the barrels of their guns?<br /> Does the shadow of the talen remain, even in direct beam of the flash-light? If so, the policemen will see something inexplicable/supernatural.<br /> What if the garou turned Crinos. Would his shadowy figure cause Delirium, even is not completely visible?<br /> Or will the talen effect cease when in bright light, for the flash-light while still mundane is a strong source of illumination causing the essence of shadow to vanish?<br /> What about the PC himself, can he end the 1h effect prematurely ?<br /> <br /> I'd love to read your opinions on the matter.<br /> As a secondary information, in the room from where the SWAT is approaching, other policemen already have two other members of the pack in homid form held at gun point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T18:41:48-07:00","id":630519,"title":"","content":"Ok I'm going to make a few assumptions for this post. If any are wrong please correct me and I'll make corrections as necessary.<br /> <br /> First if a SWAT team is clearing a building they will use flash-bang grenades upon entry. I'm guessing this happened already and the SWAT team is now in the sweep phase. This means two members per room with flashlights sweeping the area looking around at my bedroom this means a character literally had like three seconds before discovery: First remains of the talen will require a Perception+investigation roll dif. 7- SWAT is searching for a person not debris. Second no the shade Garou would not invoke the Delirium it might raise questions though like what caused the shadow. Third a mounted flashlight while being strong still depending on space will not disperse all shadows I'd leave the Shade a shade. Yes I'd allow a character to end the effect early. Personally if I was the character I'd step sideways and go for a prison break style escape of my packmates. It is a lot easier to explain a stolen vehicle ramming a police car than a torn apart SWAT team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T19:47:18-07:00","id":630575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630423-nightshade-veil-how-would-you-rule-it-works?p=630519#post630519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">First if a SWAT team is clearing a building they will use flash-bang grenades upon entry.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case they don't. It's not really common practice with SEK (Sondereinsatzkommando / which roughly is the German equivalent to SWAT). They don't have any reason to suspect anyone in the house to be armed, for example - since private gun ownership is rare.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630423-nightshade-veil-how-would-you-rule-it-works?p=630519#post630519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing this happened already and the SWAT team is now in the sweep phase. This means two members per room with flashlights sweeping the area looking around at my bedroom this means a character literally had like three seconds before discovery....</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. The character has the danger sense merit. So, when the police entered the abandoned building they squat in, they were warned. Two pack member hid in the common room, while the third barricaded himself in an adjacent room and lifted the two kin girls who were with them through a whole in the ceiling from basement level to ground level. He then heard the police enter the common room and activated the talen.<br /> <br /> But, yes, there are at least two members of the SWAT sweeping each room. The action was planned so they knew the layout of the building before they entered and planned their movements accordingly, so each they would not get separated or something like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lncbill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/630423-nightshade-veil-how-would-you-rule-it-works?p=630519#post630519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> First remains of the talen will require a Perception+investigation roll dif. 7- SWAT is searching for a person not debris. Second no the shade Garou would not invoke the Delirium it might raise questions though like what caused the shadow. Third a mounted flashlight while being strong still depending on space will not disperse all shadows I'd leave the Shade a shade. Yes I'd allow a character to end the effect early. Personally if I was the character I'd step sideways and go for a prison break style escape of my packmates. It is a lot easier to explain a stolen vehicle ramming a police car than a torn apart SWAT team.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, not sure if he thinks of it.<br /> Not sure if he has time enough to step sideways, the process can take a long time, if only a few successes are scored.<br /> <br /> The Nightshade description specifically states, that a person searching might get a roll, so - what if the police scores successes?<br /> Do they then witness something supernatural?<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean it is a general problem, with perception rolls, in my opinion. A gift like &quot;Blur of the milky eye&quot; reduced difficulty of Stealth checks, but if you want to sneak up on a group standing in an empty parking lot in broad daylight, the difficulty even with such a reduction would be high since there is no cover. The difficulty to see you would be as low as the rules permit. A gift like &quot;Invisibility&quot; on the other hand would work, for one is truly invisible. Nightshade however is unclear on the mechanics. It states one is turned into shadow (which I guess doesn't mean incorporeal nor 2-dimensional, for it would say so if it was so). But also states a person is all but invisible, which is kind of strange - since there are circumstances a shadow is pretty clearly visible - usually if there is a bright light around. And the flash-lights of the Policemen certainly count. And I don't think Nightshade is supposed to be a D&amp;D Shadowdancers &quot;hide in plain sight&quot; that allows to use stealth as long as shadow is in close proximity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-17T22:16:16-07:00","id":630701,"title":"","content":"I'd assign a difficulty of 6-8 for spotting the shadow form swinging a flashlight will cause dancing shadows so I'd assign a difficulty of 8, 7 if moving.<br /> <br /> Rational- The police are looking for a person, unless this is a Formori/Ghoul squad they would have no reason to suspect a mystical event. Further as soon as the SWAT team sees the hole in the ceiling they will race to the higher level unless the character has covered it somehow.<br /> <br /> Funny GSG-9 and the SAS are the two groups that developed the flash/bang tactic for breaching buildings that had hostages. I would've thought the police would follow a similar doctrine of a situation had escalated to the level of involving the Federal level of Law Enforcement.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T03:21:48-07:00","id":630901,"title":"","content":"Well, the police man are looking for everything. Contraband, booby traps, and what not. One of them ran into an armed animal trap when they entered the building. And there is another team sweeping the ground level, so the hole in the ceiling is surely observed, (and radioed in), for they wouldn't someone throw stuff at them, but it's not that they are in pursuit or something like that. Also, non-swat police forces are surrounding the building and once the operation had started, they activated vehicle-mounted spotlights on the outside.<br /> <br /> Also, the police here is state police. The GSG9 would indeed be German Federal Police's Counter-Terrorist and SWAT unit - previously the Federal Border Guard's. Hence the name <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>G</b></span>renz<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>s</b></span>chutz<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>g</b></span>ruppe, which is &quot;Border Protection Group&quot;.<br /> <br /> Also, I imagine, they would not &quot;swing&quot; the flashlight rapidly, but move it very steadily as they approach the room to not miss out on anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T07:50:27-07:00","id":631179,"title":"","content":"My phone won't handle the German. And I'm extremely rusty on my spelling in German. I know from my school days that the SEK used to deal with the old Baader-Meinhof group or was that a different group?<br /> This sounds very bad for the pack of Garou. I showed the question to one of my players last night as I was getting ready for work. He was very thankful that the only interaction between law enforcement and the pack involved being questioned in the deaths of a group of college students. Fortunately the character in question, the sole survivor of the pack, had a NPC or two to back up his story. The character in question was innocent of murdering the college students. That was the work of a pair of Yeren and a pair of vampires. My player said &quot;I hope someone has a lot of contacts or really high resources. &quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":293,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","user":"lncbill","date":".  fat fingered post while still typing. 08-18-2015, 11:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-18T08:14:48-07:00","id":631195,"title":"","content":"Seems your post was cut short....<br /> <br /> &quot;Sonder&quot; means special, as does &quot;Spezial&quot;. The name of german SWAT-like teams are SEK, which can mean Sondereinsatzkommando or Spezialeinsatzkommando. It's basically the same thing, but since each state can name their stuff like they want....<br /> <br /> The &quot;Bundesgrenzschutz&quot; (Federal Border Guard) was once basically that, the guards at the border. But with the EU's &quot;Schengen&quot;-Treaty there aren't usually any border guarding any more (only on the border to Switzerland). So, the Federal Government made the Federal Border Guard their own police force, which was kind of a disputed move, since the Federal government didn't have a police before and internal security is a state affair. Well, the federal ministry of the interior hadn't, the ministry for finance already had and still has their own police for custom enforcement, smuggling, product piracy, unregistered employment and all other forms of tax evasion.<br /> Well, around the same time, the Bundesbahn (Federal monopol railway) was privatised, so their own police, the Bahnpolizei, was incorporated into the Federal police aswell. But the GSG9 retained their old name, from their Bundesgrenzschutz times -&gt; <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>G</b></span>renz<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>s</b></span>chutz<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>g</b></span>ruppe, which is &quot;Border Protection Group&quot; - the S not meaning &quot;Sonder&quot; or &quot;Special&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> But back to the topic. The whole affair became kind of mood, since the PC managed to evade the cops. His alpha used Jam Technology and the few turns in total darkness were enough to flee the room.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1008,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","user":"heinrich","date":". 08-18-2015, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}